TITLE:: DrumStep
SUMMARY:: One drum-grid column, with or without a hit.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/BorderView, Classes/DrumProgrammer, Classes/GridSlider, Classes/PlayableNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DrumStep:: is one column of a LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: row. It is not a view. It holds a LINK::Classes/GridSlider::, the column start time, the drum's MIDI note number, and a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when that square is a hit. An empty square still has a step, so LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: can turn it on. The slider shows the hit's amplitude: the top of the square is CODE::1:: and the bottom is CODE::0::. Left click or left drag sets that amplitude and turns the hit on. Dragging to CODE::0::, or a right click, turns it off. LINK::#-amp_:: does the same: a mapped velocity above CODE::0:: ensures a hit, and a mapped velocity of CODE::0:: clears one. An existing hit keeps its velocity until a new amplitude is set. LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: supplies the callbacks that add and remove the note from the sequence. A row with no MIDI note number ignores both mouse buttons.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a step and its square.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
MIDI note number for this drum, or CODE::nil:: for a row that has no sound yet.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
Column start time in beats.

ARGUMENT:: palette
The LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for the square colours.

ARGUMENT:: squareSize
Width and height of the square, in pixels.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
MIDI velocity stored for a hit created without an explicit amplitude.

ARGUMENT:: hitDuration
Length of a new hit, in beats.

ARGUMENT:: addFunc
Called with the new LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when a hit is created.

ARGUMENT:: removeFunc
Called with the LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when a hit is cleared.

ARGUMENT:: existingNote
A LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: already stored for this column, or CODE::nil::. When present, the slider shows that note's amplitude and the add callback is not called.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DrumStep:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: amp_
Sets the amplitude of this column. CODE::0:: clears the hit. Any other value in CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: ensures a hit and passes the clipped value to LINK::Classes/PlayableNote#-amp_::, which sets the MIDI velocity. The slider then shows that velocity mapped back to CODE::0::–CODE::1::.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: are clipped.

METHOD:: playableNote
The LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: for this column, or CODE::nil:: when the square is empty.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: square
The square for this column.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/GridSlider::.

METHOD:: startTime
The column start time in beats.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::.

PRIVATE:: init, prClearHit, prEnsureHit, prSetAmp, prSyncSlider
